# Env

Copy to `.env` locally. After merge, Developer sets **secrets** on Railway (`TELNYX_API_KEY`, `XAI_API_KEY`, `API_KEY`, `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`). Do not place real PSTN calls from this repo. Tests mock Telnyx and xAI. Never put ElevenLabs API keys in code.

## Required for outbound calls

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `TELNYX_API_KEY` | Telnyx Call Control API (Bearer). Set on Railway after merge. |
| `XAI_API_KEY` | xAI Grok Voice Live 2. Set on Railway after merge. |
| `API_KEY` | Bearer token for `POST /api/outbound` and `GET /api/calls/:id`. Set on Railway after merge. |
| `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | Public HTTPS origin. Telnyx webhook = `{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/webhooks/telnyx`. |

## Telnyx (non-secret, TRNSF/Nuno)

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `TELNYX_CONNECTION_ID` | `3041732714274227469` | Call Control app **TRNSX-Outbound-Grok**. |
| `TELNYX_OUTBOUND_VOICE_PROFILE_ID` | `3041732644774610184` | Outbound Voice Profile bound to that app (not sent on each dial). |
| `FROM_NUMBER` | `+351210210260` | Caller ID. |

## Voice / model

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GROK_VOICE` | `ara` | Grok Voice Live 2 voice. Keep `ara` unless explicitly overridden. |
| `GROK_MODEL` | `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0` | Grok Voice Live 2 model. |
| `GROK_VOICE_SPEED` | `1.05` | Documented xAI `audio.output.speed` (0.7–1.5). Slight liveliness nudge above the API default `1.0`. **Do not change.** |

## ElevenLabs (stub — dual-ready)

Not wired into the audio pipeline yet. Grok voice stays **`ara`**. Developer sets `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` on Railway after merge (secret — never in git).

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | _(empty)_ | Secret. Required before `tts_provider=elevenlabs` is accepted (`ready.elevenlabs`). |
| `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID` | `tnL8F53kfXcNNVSwbLzy` | IVC cloned female voice. Nuno may swap later. |
| `ELEVENLABS_MODEL` | `eleven_v3` | Preferred model. Vault had `multilingual_v2` — do not default to that. |

If `POST /api/outbound` sends `tts_provider: "elevenlabs"` without `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, the API returns **503 `elevenlabs_not_configured`**. When the key is set, `ready.elevenlabs` is true and the call is accepted; audio still goes through Grok `ara` until the TTS pipeline is wired.

Language on each call: `pt-PT` | `en-GB` | `en-US` (default `pt-PT` if omitted).

Persona (`persona` or `greeting`) and `objective` come from `POST /api/outbound`. There is no branded spoken default and no recording notice. If both `persona` and `greeting` are omitted, the service composes `Olá`/`Hello` + Lisbon time-of-day + **caller identity** («Ligo da secretária.») + a short natural ask derived from `objective` (never a ROLEPLAY/prompt dump, never «bem-vindo ao restaurante»). Optional `spokenAsk` is a clean one-line ask. Optional `timezone` (IANA, default `Europe/Lisbon`) selects the local clock. `waitForCallee` does not require `greeting`.

## Turn-taking (Grok server_vad)

Phone-tuned so the agent answers promptly after the callee stops (default 160ms silence). The Telnyx↔Grok bridge forwards audio immediately (no extra debounce after `speech_stopped`). Override if needed:

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GROK_VAD_THRESHOLD` | `0.5` | VAD activation (`0.1`–`0.9`). |
| `GROK_VAD_SILENCE_MS` | `160` | End-of-turn silence in ms before the model replies. Keep at 160 — lower values can chop barge-in. |
| `GROK_VAD_PREFIX_PADDING_MS` | `200` | Audio kept before detected speech start (barge-in). |
| `GROK_VAD_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` | `12000` | Idle timeout (not the turn gap). |
| `GROK_CALLEE_SPEECH_GRACE_MS` | `500` | After answer/stream start, ignore `speech_started` (ringback/noise) before waitForCallee can unlock via duration. Word-length speech during grace unlocks as soon as this window ends (or sooner on transcript). |
| `GROK_CALLEE_MIN_SPEECH_MS` | `80` | Minimum accepted utterance length after grace (waitForCallee). Short greetings («estou», «estou?», «alô», «sim») and any non-empty transcript unlock immediately. |
| `GROK_HANGUP_PLAYOUT_MS` | `1000` | Extra Telnyx playout after Grok `response.done` before hangup on `end_call`. |

## Optional

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `RESULT_WEBHOOK` | `POST` JSON when a call ends. Empty disables. |
| `TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY` | Account Ed25519 public key. When set, `/webhooks/telnyx` verifies signatures. |
| `XAI_BASE_URL` | Default `https://api.x.ai`. |
| `TELNYX_API_BASE` | Default `https://api.telnyx.com`. |
| `PORT` | Railway injects this. Default `3000`. |
| `MAX_CALL_SECONDS` | Hard cap before hangup. Default `600`. |

This service is **outbound-only** and is **not** Alice.
